Headless: download the map the game offers, and hear how it ended

A game offers its map with GMCP's Client.Map, which the GUI's mapper turns into a "Download from game" button, and
TMap::downloadMap() then says how the download went only in the main console, which an app over THeadlessSession
does not show. This adds THeadlessSession::offeredMapUrl() and downloadOfferedMap(), with offeredMapChanged as the
game offers one and mapDownloadFinished once a download has ended, loaded or not with the console's message as the
reason, after its mapProgressFinished. TMap gets signal_mapDownloadFinished(), sent once for each download it began,
and downloadMap() answers whether it began one. Neither TMap::setMmpMapLocation()'s debug log nor the console's messages of a failed
download show the user name and password a game can put in the URL any more.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.

